  "answer": "## What to fix first\n\n1. **Reflected XSS on /search** -- Lies on a length-6 path from GET /search to Customer database (score 12.75).\n   Path: ep:search -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:xss -> (GRANTS) -> id:user -> (CAN_ACCESS) -> asset:api -> (EXPOSES) -> ep:orders -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:idor -> (LEADS_TO) -> asset:db\n   Contextual output encoding for every sink, a strict Content-Security-Policy, HttpOnly cookies, and framework auto-escaping; sanitise HTML with a vetted library.\n\n2. **IDOR on /api/orders** -- Lies on a length-6 path from GET /search to Customer database (score 12.75).\n   Path: ep:search -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:xss -> (GRANTS) -> id:user -> (CAN_ACCESS) -> asset:api -> (EXPOSES) -> ep:orders -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:idor -> (LEADS_TO) -> asset:db\n   Enforce object-level authorization on every access (the resource must belong to the caller); use unguessable references and check ownership server-side.\n\n3. **Auth bypass on /login** -- Lies on a length-6 path from POST /login to Customer database (score 9.92).\n   Path: ep:login -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:authbypass -> (GRANTS) -> id:user -> (CAN_ACCESS) -> asset:api -> (EXPOSES) -> ep:orders -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:idor -> (LEADS_TO) -> asset:db\n   Enforce function-level authorization server-side on every privileged action (deny-by-default); never rely on UI hiding. Verify role on the endpoint, not the client.\n\n4. **Open redirect on /go** -- Lies on a length-6 path from GET /go to Customer database (score 8.50).\n   Path: ep:go -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:redirect -> (GRANTS) -> id:user -> (CAN_ACCESS) -> asset:api -> (EXPOSES) -> ep:orders -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:idor -> (LEADS_TO) -> asset:db\n   Use an allow-list of redirect targets or relative paths only; never redirect to a user-supplied absolute URL.\n\n5. **SSRF on /metrics** -- Lies on a length-6 path from GET /metrics to Customer database (score 7.08).\n   Path: ep:metrics -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:ssrf -> (LEADS_TO) -> asset:admin -> (CONNECTS_TO) -> asset:api -> (EXPOSES) -> ep:orders -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:idor -> (LEADS_TO) -> asset:db\n   Enforce an egress allow-list, resolve-and-pin destinations, block link-local/metadata ranges, disable unused URL schemes, and enforce IMDSv2.\n\n6. **Mass assignment on /admin** -- Lies on a length-6 path from GET /metrics to Customer database (score 5.00).\n   Path: ep:metrics -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:ssrf -> (LEADS_TO) -> asset:admin -> (EXPOSES) -> ep:adminapi -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:massassign -> (GRANTS) -> id:admin -> (CAN_ACCESS) -> asset:db\n   Bind only an explicit allow-list of fields to models; never auto-bind request bodies to privileged attributes (role, isAdmin, price).\n\n7. **SQLi on /admin** -- Lies on a length-5 path from GET /metrics to Customer database (score 4.00).\n   Path: ep:metrics -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:ssrf -> (LEADS_TO) -> asset:admin -> (EXPOSES) -> ep:adminapi -> (HAS_FINDING) -> f:sqli -> (LEADS_TO) -> asset:db\n   Use parameterised queries / prepared statements everywhere; never concatenate input into SQL; apply least-privilege DB accounts.\n\n## Choke point\nFix **IDOR on /api/orders** -> severs **4 of 6** paths to Customer database, including the highest-value one."
